</Group>
<Group labelreference="L477" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Notice that we have written the tableau in two ways; the second just has blanks where all the zeros reside and is how the tableau is usually written in books. Now, how do we choose the remaining coefficients in the Butcher tableau? The idea is to select them in such a way that the one-step error in the stencil is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, where <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> characterizes a specified global error; that is,</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" alignment="centred"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">More concretely, to determine the coefficients we need to do the following:</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal"></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" initial="-1" bulletsuffix="." bullet="numeric">Construct an expression for the local error by first subtracting the right-hand side from the left-hand side of <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">evolve</Font>, subbing in the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEibkYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEibkYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation> definitions and then making the substitutions <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" initial="-1" bulletsuffix="." bullet="numeric">Expand the result in a Taylor series in <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiaEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, and simplify derivatives using the differential equation <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" initial="-1" bulletsuffix="." bullet="numeric">Select <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> in such a way that the coefficients of all terms<Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> with <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> are zero. Note that our choices have to work for all possible forms of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" bulletsuffix="."></Text-field><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal" bulletsuffix=".">Obviously, we want to choose <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> as big as possible in order minimize the one-step error. It turns out that for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, there are enough coefficents in the Butcher tableau to achieve <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, but for higher <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, the global error cannot be made that small. In the following sections, we will construct explicit Runge-Kutta stencils for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> and choose <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">The <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> (Huen or modified Euler) method</Text-field></Title>
<Group labelreference="L456" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L494" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">In this section, we will construct an example of an <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> explicit Runge-Kutta stencil. The relevant equations are (see previous section) the following.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L491" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">M := 2;

for n from 1 to M do:
    for m from n to M do:
        alpha[n, m] := 0:
    od:
od;

c[1] := 0;

for n from 1 to M do:
    k_def[n] := k[n] = f(x[i]+c[n]*h, y[i]+h*add(alpha[n, m]*k[m], m = 1..M)):
od;

evolve := y[i+1] = y[i]+h*add(b[n]*k[n], n = 1..M);

A := Matrix([seq([seq(alpha[n, m], m = 1..M)], n = 1..M)]):
B := Vector[row]([seq(b[n], n = 1..M)]):
C := Vector[column]([seq(c[n], n = 1..M)]):
Butcher := map(x -&gt; if x = 0 then `` else x end if, Matrix([[C, A], [``, B]]));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJNR0YoIiIjNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
