</Group>
<Group labelreference="L442" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This expression has no reference to the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEibkYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUklbXN1YkdGJDYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEia0YnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUYjNiYtRi82JlEibkYnRjJGNUY4RjJGNUY4LyUvc3Vic2NyaXB0c2hpZnRHUSIwRidGNS9GOVEnbm9ybWFsRic=</Equation>'s. Note we could have generated the error in a single line by recursively subbing in <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">k_def</Font> using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">$</Font> operator. It is not hard to convince yourself that the number of times <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">k_def</Font> needs to be subsituted in for an <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>-stage method is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, so we take that into account in our code.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L434" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Error := subs(convert(k_def, list)$M, (lhs-rhs)(evolve));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L416" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, we need to replace the numeric data with the exact function values they are meant to represent:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L412" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Subs := {y[i] = y(x), y[i+1] = y(x+h), x[i] = x};
Error := subs(Subs, Error);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSVTdWJzR0YoPCUvJkkieEdGKDYjSSJpR0YoRjEvJkkieUdGKEYyLUY2NiNGMS8mRjY2IywmRjMiIiJGPUY9LUY2NiMsJkYxRj1JImhHRihGPTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L418" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We then expand the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Error</Font> in a Taylor series of order <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L415" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">Error := series(Error, h, M+1);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L426" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We have not yet used the fact that <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQEYyRkA=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQEYyRkA=</Equation> is the solution to <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. We can use this to remove the derivatives of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQEYyRkA=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYmLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQEYyRkA=</Equation> appearing above.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L422" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">derivative[1] := D(y)(x) = f(x, y(x));
for j from 2 to M do:
    derivative[j] := subs(derivative[1], convert(diff(derivative[j-1], x), D)): 
od;

Error := subs(convert(derivative, list), Error);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkrZGVyaXZhdGl2ZUdGKDYjIiIiLy0tSSJER0YlNiNJInlHRig2I0kieEdGKC1JImZHRig2JEY4LUY2Rjc3I0Yx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+JkkrZGVyaXZhdGl2ZUdGKDYjIiIjLy0tLUkjQEBHRiU2JEkiREdGJUYwNiNJInlHRig2I0kieEdGKCwmLS0mRjc2IyIiIjYjSSJmR0YoNiRGOy1GOUY6RkEqJi0tJkY3Ri9GQkZERkEtRkNGREZBRkE3I0Yx</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L427" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, to determine what conditions the coefficients need to satisfy for the error to be <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, we can rearrange this expression to be a polynomial in <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> This can be accomplished using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">collect</Font> command, but we first need to write down a set corresponding to the terms we want to collect together. To do so, let us first get a set with all the indeterminants in <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Error</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L428" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">vars := indets(Error);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSV2YXJzR0YoPCxJImhHRihJInhHRigmSSZhbHBoYUdGKDYkIiIjIiIiJkkiYkdGKDYjRjUmRjc2I0Y0JkkiY0dGKEY6LUkiZkdGKDYkRjAtSSJ5R0YoNiNGMEZALS0mSSJER0YlRjg2I0Y+Rj8tLSZGRkY6RkdGPzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L430" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Now, we subtract out the unknown coefficients.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L425" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">vars := vars minus unknowns;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSV2YXJzR0YoPChJImhHRihJInhHRigtSSJmR0YoNiRGMC1JInlHRig2I0YwRjQtLSZJIkRHRiU2IyIiIjYjRjJGMy0tJkY6NiMiIiNGPUYzNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L429" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Finally, there is no need to factor over <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieEYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation> or <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYnLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQC1GLDYlUSFGJ0YvRjVGMkZA">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYnLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEieUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnLUkobWZlbmNlZEdGJDYlLUYjNiUtRiw2JlEieEYnRi9GMkY1RjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYnRjJGQC1GLDYlUSFGJ0YvRjVGMkZA</Equation>, so we take these out, and the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">indets</Font> function does not count the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> term as an indeterminant, so we add it back in.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L423" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">vars := vars minus {x, y(x)};
vars := vars union {O(h^(M+1))};</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSV2YXJzR0YoPCZJImhHRigtSSJmR0YoNiRJInhHRigtSSJ5R0YoNiNGMy0tJkkiREdGJTYjIiIiNiNGMUYyLS0mRjo2IyIiI0Y9RjI3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSV2YXJzR0YoPCdJImhHRigtSSJPR0YlNiMqJEYvIiIkLUkiZkdGKDYkSSJ4R0YoLUkieUdGKDYjRjgtLSZJIkRHRiU2IyIiIjYjRjZGNy0tJkY/NiMiIiNGQkY3NyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L432" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We can rewrite <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Error</Font> as a polynomial now in all the unique combinations of the terms in <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">vars</Font> using <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">collect</Font>. However, <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">collect</Font> works best on simple sums (i.e., objects of Maple type <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">`+`</Font>) as opposed to series (i.e., objects of Maple type <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">series</Font>), so we convert <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Error</Font> before collecting.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L433" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">whattype(Error);
Error := convert(Error, `+`);
whattype(Error);
Error := collect(Error, vars, distributed);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVEnc2VyaWVzRicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSV0cnVlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0Yn">SSdzZXJpZXNHJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRH</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbWlHNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JVEkYCtgRicvJSdpdGFsaWNHUSV0cnVlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0Yn">SSIrRyUqcHJvdGVjdGVkRw==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L438" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">distributed</Font> option ensures that the coefficients of the resulting polynomial will only involve elements of the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">unknowns</Font> set. We can put each of the coefficients in the polynomial into a set using <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">coeffs</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L431" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sys := {coeffs(Error, vars)};</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzeXNHRig8JiIiIiwmI0YvIiIjRi8qJiZJImJHRig2I0YyRi8mSSZhbHBoYUdGKDYkRjJGL0YvISIiLCZGMUYvKiZGNEYvJkkiY0dGKEY2Ri9GOiwoJkY1NiNGL0Y6RjRGOkYvRi83I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L439" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Actually, this set includes the coefficient of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, which is just <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation>. We are not really interested in this, so we remove it from the list. After this, we set each coefficient equal to zero to yield a system of equations for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L479" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sys := sys minus {1};
sys := map(x -&gt; x = 0, sys);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzeXNHRig8JSwmIyIiIiIiI0YxKiYmSSJiR0YoNiNGMkYxJkkmYWxwaGFHRig2JEYyRjFGMSEiIiwmRjBGMSomRjRGMSZJImNHRihGNkYxRjosKCZGNTYjRjFGOkY0RjpGMUYxNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzeXNHRig8JS8sJiMiIiIiIiNGMiomJkkiYkdGKDYjRjNGMiZJJmFscGhhR0YoNiRGM0YyRjIhIiIiIiEvLCZGMUYyKiZGNUYyJkkiY0dGKEY3RjJGO0Y8LywoJkY2NiNGMkY7RjVGO0YyRjJGPDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L446" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We can try to attempt to solve this system.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L448" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sol := solve(sys);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRig8Ji8mSSZhbHBoYUdGKDYkIiIjIiIiLCQqJCZJImJHRig2I0YzISIiI0Y0RjMvJkY4NiNGNCwmRjdGOkY0RjQvRjdGNy8mSSJjR0YoRjlGNTcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L453" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We actually fail to get a definate solution and rather get a one-parameter family of solutions. This is because the system of equations is actually underdetermined; there are many possible solutions. All of these solutions will generate a valid, explicit <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation>-stage Runge-Kutta stencil, which can be seen if we put <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">sol</Font> into <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">Error</Font>.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L455" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs(sol, Error);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkiT0c2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjKiRJImhHRiciIiQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L413" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Stated another way, there is no unique <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiMkYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation>-stage explicit Runge-Kutta method. However, to use the method, we do need actual values for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, so we need to make a choice. The customary additional assumption is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, which yields a definitive answer for the other constants.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L435" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">assumptions := {b[2] = 1/2};
solution := solve(subs(assumptions, sys));
answer := assumptions union solution;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSxhc3N1bXB0aW9uc0dGKDwjLyZJImJHRig2IyIiIyMiIiJGMzcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSlzb2x1dGlvbkdGKDwlLyZJJmFscGhhR0YoNiQiIiMiIiJGNC8mSSJiR0YoNiNGNCNGNEYzLyZJImNHRig2I0YzRjQ3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdhbnN3ZXJHRig8Ji8mSSZhbHBoYUdGKDYkIiIjIiIiRjQvJkkiYkdGKDYjRjQjRjRGMy8mRjc2I0YzRjkvJkkiY0dGKEY8RjQ3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L419" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This is known to generate the Heun or modified Euler stencil. Its Butcher tableau is</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L411" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs(answer, Butcher);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyNYLCUhR0YoRihbZ2whIiUhISEjKiIkIiQtSSNtaUc2JEYmL0krbW9kdWxlbmFtZUdGKEYkNiNRI2BgRigtSSNtbkdGMDYjUSIxRihGLkYuRjUtSSZtZnJhY0dGMDYkRjUtRjY2I1EiMkYoRi5GLkY5NyMtSSdNYXRyaXhHRiU2Iy9JJCVpZEdGKCI1KyZRVStfIilbJCpvJA==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L447" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Finally, the actual equations one uses in a numerical method are the following:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L417" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">for n from 1 to M do:
    subs(answer, k_def[n]):
od;
subs(answer, evolve);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LyZJImtHNiI2IyIiIi1JImZHRiU2JCZJInhHRiU2I0kiaUdGJSZJInlHRiVGLQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LyZJImtHNiI2IyIiIy1JImZHRiU2JCwmSSJoR0YlIiIiJkkieEdGJTYjSSJpR0YlRi0sJiomRixGLSZGJDYjRi1GLUYtJkkieUdGJUYwRi0=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LyZJInlHNiI2IywmSSJpR0YlIiIiRilGKSwmJkYkNiNGKEYpKiZJImhHRiVGKSwmJkkia0dGJTYjRikjRikiIiMmRjE2I0Y0RjNGKUYp</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L443" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Moreover, the one-step error is</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L445" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">subs(answer, Error);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkiT0c2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjKiRJImhHRiciIiQ=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L454" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Notice that the Huen method gives the same one-step accuracy as the trapezoidal method, but it is fully explicit.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 1" layout="Heading 1">The classic fourth order Runge-Kutta scheme</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L436" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">restart;
Digits := 14;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSdEaWdpdHNHRigiIzk3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L451" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We now turn our attention to an explicit <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiNEYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiNEYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation>-stage Runge-Kutta method. Note that the code from the previous section works for any value of <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbWlHRiQ2JlEiTUYnLyUnaXRhbGljR1EldHJ1ZUYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ2l0YWxpY0YnRjIvRjZRJ25vcm1hbEYn</Equation>, so we could just rerun it to obtain the equations satisfied by <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> when <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. However, we can take this opportunity to rewrite the code a little more compactly.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L457" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">M := 4;

for n from 1 to M do:
    for m from n to M do:
        alpha[n, m] := 0:
    od:
od:

c[1] := 0:

for n from 1 to M do:
    k_def[n] := k[n] = f(x[i]+c[n]*h, y[i]+h*add(alpha[n, m]*k[m], m = 1..M)):
od:

evolve := y[i+1] = y[i]+h*add(b[n]*k[n], n = 1..M):
unknowns := {seq(seq(alpha[n, m], m = 1..n-1), n = 2..M), seq(b[n], n = 1..M), seq(c[n], n = 2..M)}:

derivative[1] := D(y)(x) = f(x, y(x)):
for j from 2 to M do:
    derivative[j] := subs(derivative[1], convert(diff(derivative[j-1], x), D)):
od:

Subs := {y[i] = y(x), y[i+1] = y(x+h), x[i] = x}:
Error := subs(convert(derivative, list), convert(series(subs(convert(k_def, list)$M, Subs, (lhs-rhs)(evolve)), h, M+1), `+`)):
vars := indets(Error) minus unknowns minus {x, y(x)}:
sys := {coeffs(collect(Error, vars, distributed), vars)} minus {1}:
sys := map(x -&gt; simplify(x = 0), sys);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSJNR0YoIiIlNyNGLg==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L449" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This is the set of equations that must be satisfied by <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> to have a valid <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiNEYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEiNEYnLyUrZXhlY3V0YWJsZUdRJmZhbHNlRicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYnRi9GMg==</Equation>-stage stencil. We can now ask Maple to solve this system of equations. I have supressed the output as it is very long. (<Font italic="true">Warning:</Font> the following step takes about <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display="LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEjMTVGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJ0YvRjI=">LUklbXJvd0c2Iy9JK21vZHVsZW5hbWVHNiJJLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nR0koX3N5c2xpYkdGJzYlLUkjbW5HRiQ2JVEjMTVGJy8lK2V4ZWN1dGFibGVHUSZmYWxzZUYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJ0YvRjI=</Equation> seconds on my machine. If you execute it on your computer, the number printed out is how much CPU time you used. See <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">?time()</Font> for more details.)</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L486" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">st := time():
rk4_solutions := {solve(sys)}:
time()-st;</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEnMTUuMTk3RicvJSxtYXRodmFyaWFudEdRJ25vcm1hbEYn">JCImKD46ISIk</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L484" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The number of classes of solutions returned by <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">solve</Font> can be obtained using the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">nops</Font> command:</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L458" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">NN := nops(rk4_solutions);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSNOTkdGKCIiKDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L482" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here is an example of class of solutions.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L460" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">rk4_solutions[1];</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">PC8vJkkmYWxwaGFHNiI2JCIiIyIiIiNGKUYoLyZGJTYkIiIkRiksJCokJkYlNiQiIiVGLiEiIiNGNEYoLyZGJTYkRi5GKCwkRjBGKi8mRiU2JEYzRiksJkYxRjRGNUYpLyZGJTYkRjNGKCNGLkYoL0YxRjEvJkkiYkdGJjYjRiksJiNGKSIiJ0YpRjEjRjRGSS8mRkU2I0YoI0YoRi4vJkZFNiNGLiwkRjFGSC8mRkU2I0YzRkgvJkkiY0dGJkZNRiovJkZYRlEiIiEvJkZYRlVGKQ==</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L489" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This is a parameteric solution; i.e., just as in the <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> case, there are an infinite number of solutions for <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. The &quot;classic fourth order Runge-Kutta method&quot; involves the following assumptions.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L464" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">assumptions := {alpha[4, 1] = 0, alpha[3, 1] = 0, alpha[4, 2] = 0, b[4] = b[1], b[3] = b[2]};</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSxhc3N1bXB0aW9uc0dGKDwnLyZJJmFscGhhR0YoNiQiIiQiIiIiIiEvJkYxNiQiIiVGNEY1LyZGMTYkRjkiIiNGNS8mSSJiR0YoNiNGMyZGQDYjRj0vJkZANiNGOSZGQDYjRjQ3I0Yu</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L500" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">This leads to the following solution for the coefficients.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L495" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">sol := solve(subs(assumptions, sys));
answer := sol union subs(sol, assumptions);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LV9JLFR5cGVzZXR0aW5nRzYkJSpwcm90ZWN0ZWRHSShfc3lzbGliRzYiSSxtcHJpbnRzbGFzaEdGKDYkNyM+SSRzb2xHRig8Ki8mSSZhbHBoYUdGKDYkIiIjIiIiI0Y0RjMvJkYxNiQiIiRGM0Y1LyZGMTYkIiIlRjlGNC8mSSJiR0YoNiNGNCNGNCIiJy8mRkA2I0YzI0Y0RjkvJkkiY0dGKEZGRjUvJkZKNiNGOUY1LyZGSjYjRj1GNDcjRi4=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L470" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The Butcher tableau for this stencil is as follows.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L487" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">A := Matrix([seq([seq(alpha[n, m], m = 1..M)], n = 1..M)]):
B := Vector[row]([seq(b[n], n = 1..M)]):
C := Vector[column]([seq(c[n], n = 1..M)]):
Butcher = subs(answer, map(x -&gt; if x = 0 then `` else x end if, Matrix([[C, A], [``, B]])));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L472" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">Here are the basic equations.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L473" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">rk4 := subs(answer, [seq(k_def[n], n = 1..M), evolve]);</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L471" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We can confirm that the one-step error is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation> as expected.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L469" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">simplify(subs(answer, Error));</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="">LUkiT0c2JCUqcHJvdGVjdGVkR0koX3N5c2xpYkc2IjYjKiRJImhHRiciIiY=</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group labelreference="L461" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">We conclude by writing a procedure that makes use of the classic Runge-Kutta method to solve <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>. We first transform the <Font style="Maple Input" executable="false">rk4</Font> stencil into a set of mappings.</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L402" drawlabel="true">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal">for n from 1 to M+1 do:
    K[n] := unapply(rhs(rk4[n]), h, x[i], y[i], seq(k[m], m = 1..n-1));
od;</Text-field>
